"""Build a topic reference for the project viva using python-docx."""
from docx import Document
from docx.shared import Pt
from pathlib import Path

topics=[
("Architecture","The pipeline separates receipt from processing.","A successful upload can still contain an invalid PDF.","The API creates metadata, Storage emits an event and the worker commits the result.","infra/bootstrap.py","Browser → API → Storage → Eventarc → processor → Firestore and Logging","Open a generated PDF's detail page and compare its four history entries.","What proves processing finished?","The final Processed history entry and the extracted page count."),
("Frontend","Six same-origin HTML pages use ES modules.","Students can inspect each request without a build tool.","Shared CSS tokens style the pages. XMLHttpRequest tracks byte progress. Polling retrieves current metadata.","frontend/js/app.js","The UI uses the authenticated API and formats timestamps in Asia/Kolkata.","Upload two synthetic files, follow one result, then filter the list.","Does a full progress bar imply processing succeeded?","It measures network transfer. The document's status comes from Firestore."),
("Backend","The Flask API owns HTTP requests from the browser.","It centralizes auth, quick validation and data access.","A Flask factory registers the API blueprint. Gunicorn serves the container on loopback through Compose.","backend/app.py","The API talks to Storage and Firestore using emulator endpoints.","Inspect a 201 response from POST /api/documents.","What does the returned ID identify?","One upload and its history, even when another file shares its name."),
("Authentication","One shared local account uses an opaque session cookie.","The browser needs authenticated access without knowing emulator credentials.","bcrypt verifies the password. SQLite stores session identity, CSRF token and idle expiry.","backend/app.py","The before-request checkpoint protects all private API routes.","Open the dashboard in a private window, then sign in as demo.","What happens after logout?","The server removes the old session and issues an anonymous one."),
("Database structure","Firestore stores documents, history, idempotency records and audit entries.","Queries can retrieve metadata without reading PDF bytes.","The API creates the document and initial history atomically. The worker checks state and attempt within transactions.","docs/metadata-schema.md","History belongs to the document; audit records survive deletion.","Compare the IDs in after/event-trace.json and after/replay.json under evidence/.","Where are the PDF bytes?","Only in the private storage object."),
("Document metadata","Each record tracks identity, state, timing and parser results.","A reviewer can trace one upload from receipt to its outcome.","The API assigns ID, safe key and owner. The processor adds hash, page count, version, warnings and attempt result.","processor/app.py","The UI reads this record through GET /api/documents/{id}.","View two identical uploads and compare their IDs and hashes.","Why allow equal hashes?","Every submission has a separate lifecycle and a visible duplicate-content indicator."),
("Cloud Storage","The GCS emulator stores objects under generated keys.","Users must download through the authorized application.","The Python SDK uses a Floci-issued token. The Compose cloud service enforces IAM and stays on the private network.","infra/cloud.py","An object finalized event carries a generated name and storage generation.","Read evidence/setup/sdk-probe.txt and stream a download from the UI.","Can anonymous users read through the tested REST endpoint?","The anonymous object probe returned HTTP 403."),
("Firestore","The metadata service supports document writes and conditional transitions.","Concurrent deliveries should not advance a terminal state twice.","The SDK transaction reads status and attempt before updating the document and appending history.","processor/app.py","The list, detail and dashboard routes read the resulting documents.","Run tests/verify.py and inspect the unchanged replay snapshots.","What if an old completion arrives late?","The expected-state comparison rejects it."),
("Cloud Run","Cloud Run is the intended processor host.","The official architecture separates processing from the web request.","This configuration uses a Compose worker because the Floci runtime deployment reported a missing socket.","compose.yaml","Eventarc reaches the same Flask event handler via its internal HTTP endpoint.","Show the integration page and evidence/setup/cloud-run.json.","Was Cloud Run execution verified?","The control plane accepted the request; the runtime failed. Hosting is labelled Simulated."),
("Eventarc","The event router forwards object finalization to the processor.","Processing starts asynchronously after the object write.","Bootstrap installs a trigger matching the configured bucket and finalized event type. The worker reads binary CloudEvent headers.","infra/bootstrap.py","The HTTP body carries object identity and generation.","Upload a PDF and correlate its timeline with the processing log.","Who triggers normal processing?","The emulator's Eventarc service delivers the HTTP request."),
("Cloud Logging","Cloud Logging stores operational events.","Reviewers need evidence of decisions and failures without inspecting files.","The shared logger constructs an allowlisted record, emits JSON and submits it to the emulator's entries write endpoint.","infra/cloud.py","API upload and processor completion/failure events use the file ID to correlate stages.","Compare evidence/setup/logging.txt and evidence/after/redacted.jsonl.","What stays out of the log?","Original names, PDF bytes, credentials, passwords, cookies and tokens."),
("Floci","Floci GCP emulates cloud service protocols locally.","The team can test real client operations on a laptop.","Compose pins the tested GCP image digest. IAM enforcement protects the application REST storage path.","compose.yaml","Official Google Python clients use the internal cloud host.","Run docker compose ps -a and show the SDK probe evidence.","Does listing a service prove it works?","Only a successful operation with its observed output supports that claim."),
("PDF validation","Validation occurs at intake and after storage.","Filename and MIME checks cannot establish a valid PDF structure.","The API counts streamed bytes and checks type. The processor checks signature, pages, encryption and warnings.","processor/parse_input.py","The worker reads the exact object generation and writes the parser result to Firestore.","Upload corrupt.pdf, encrypted.pdf and marker.pdf from generated samples.","Does the marker execute?","The parser inspects structural objects only. The worker records a warning."),
("Event processing","One delivery supplies object identity and a trigger identifier.","A worker can locate the correct bytes without using a display label.","The worker validates the generated key and bucket, claims the attempt and reads the generation.","processor/app.py","Firestore history connects the event to the terminal result.","Compare event-trace.json to the detail history.","Why keep a generation?","It identifies the object version for the read."),
("Idempotency","A replay must leave completed work unchanged.","Event delivery may occur more than once.","Expected-state and attempt checks prevent duplicate state transitions. A persisted claim records event identity and outcome.","tests/verify.py","Reprocess allocates a fresh attempt, whereas a replay uses the existing event.","Compare before and after in evidence/after/replay.json.","What was compared?","The complete document metadata and ordered history."),
("Failure handling","Permanent validation failures end an attempt; transient failures allow bounded retries.","Users need a visible explanation and a controlled recovery action.","The worker records failure codes, retries temporary exceptions and supports manual reprocessing through the API.","tests/reliability.py","The UI displays failure reason, attempt count and previous history.","Read the forced failure evidence, then reprocess a failed PDF.","How were transient errors tested?","A fixture injected two timeouts before success and checked retry history."),
("Security","The application protects local demo data at several boundaries.","A shared demo account still needs private storage, safe names and protected writes.","Server-side sessions, CSRF tokens, generated keys, parser isolation, rate limits and structured logs implement the controls.","docs/security-controls.md","Input validation precedes storage and content parsing runs in the processor.","Inspect evidence/after/security.json and run the local suite.","Can this handle sensitive real records?","This project is scoped to synthetic local data and one shared account."),
("Testing","The suite compares observed behavior against defined outcomes.","Implementation alone cannot demonstrate replay safety or visible failure.","The PowerShell runner executes live HTTP and worker checks, records a matrix, then tests extra fixtures.","scripts/run-all-tests.ps1","Checks exercise the actual local API, emulator and processor; fault injection isolates particular error paths.","Run the script and review matrix.md, security.json and reliability.txt.","What is simulated in testing?","Temporary storage exceptions and a controlled failure are injected explicitly."),
("Deployment","Compose starts and connects the local services.","The five students need a repeatable Windows setup.","Setup builds a non-root Python image, generates the local login and runs the bootstrap job.","scripts/setup.ps1","Private service names connect API, cloud and processor; only the API publishes a loopback port.","From a clone, run setup.ps1 and visit the address in README.md.","What does a zero exit from bootstrap mean?","Bucket and event trigger configuration succeeded.")
]
d=Document()
d.add_heading("DocuFlow technical reference",0)
d.add_paragraph("Use one topic per review discussion. Each page identifies the implementation, its evidence and a question a reviewer can use to test understanding.")
for i,t in enumerate(topics):
    if i:d.add_page_break()
    d.add_heading(t[0],1)
    for title,body in zip(("What it is","Why it matters","Implementation","Code location","Interaction","Demonstration","Reviewer question","Answer"),t[1:]):
        p=d.add_paragraph()
        p.add_run(title+"   ").bold=True
        p.add_run(body)
d.save(Path("docs")/"Technical-reference.docx")
